# Generated by ../hen_tag_enclosure.py and ../cap_marking.py.
#
# The stable printables (body, cap, fit coupons) ARE committed, so the parts can
# be printed without setting up the CAD toolchain. Everything below is either a
# debugging aid or produced per tag on demand, and would only churn the history.

# Half sections and the board stand-in: inspection only, never printed.
section_*.stl
board_mock.stl

# Per-tag caps: one set per hen, regenerate with `cap_marking.py <number>`.
cap_[0-9]*.stl
marking_*.stl
core_*.stl
cap_*.3mf

# ...except one worked sample pair, kept as the reference for what the feature does.
!cap_67.3mf
!cap_67_P1S.3mf

# Bambu Studio CLI side effects of slice_check.py: never printed, never committed.
result.json
slice/

# Stable data asset for the app preview (hen-cap-layout/1), regenerated by cap_svg.py.
!layout.json
# Preview/proof scratch renders.
proof_*.svg
preview_test.svg
test_plate.3mf
slice_test/
plates/
plates_test/
cache/
proof/
full_plate.json
full_plate.log
